+## Context
+
+`TaskList.add` already validates title, priority and tags and rejects duplicate titles, returning a `Result`. The import only has to parse lines and delegate.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** one public `importTasks(list, text)`; per-line report; reuse of `add`'s validation and messages.
+**Non-Goals:** quoting or escaping `;` in titles, other separators, header rows, updating existing tasks, all-or-nothing import.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Placement:** `src/domain/import.ts` holds a pure `parseTaskLine(line): Result<NewTask>` and `importTasks(list, text)`. Parsing a line fails with `invalid-input` for more than three fields. `src/index.ts` re-exports `importTasks` and the type `ImportResult`/`ImportRejection`.
+- **Delegation to `add`:** each parsed line calls `list.add`; its error message becomes the `reason`. No new error code, no throw, no clock (the list's clock stamps the tasks). A failed `add` leaves the list unchanged already.
+- **Parsing:** split text on `\r?\n`; skip lines that are blank after trimming; split the rest on `;`. Fields are trimmed; empty priority means `normal`; tags are split on runs of whitespace with empties dropped. The priority is not case-folded (`High` is rejected as invalid) to stay consistent with `add`.
+- **Line numbers:** the index in the split text plus one, so blank lines count.
+- **Duplicates within the text** are handled naturally, as the first one is already in the list when the second is added.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- A title containing `;` cannot be imported; it is rejected as having too many fields, with a clear reason.
