+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from their spreadsheets and have lists of tasks to bring in. Adding them one by one through `add` is slow, and one bad row should not stop the rest.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `importTasks(list, text)`, a public helper that reads one task per line as `title;priority;tags` and adds every valid line to the list.
+- It returns `{ imported, rejected }`: how many tasks were added, and each line that could not be added as `{ line, reason }`, with `line` counting from 1.
+- Blank lines are skipped (but still counted in line numbers). An empty priority means `normal`; tags are separated by spaces.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `bulk-task-import`: importing many tasks from text, one per line, with a report of what was added and what was rejected.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None: each line goes through the existing `add`, so the rules in `task-input-validation` and the duplicate-title rule apply unchanged.
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/domain/import.ts` with the parsing and the import; `src/index.ts` exports `importTasks` and its result types (the public API changes by addition only).
+- New tests in `test/`.
+- Project rules: no new dependency; TSDoc on the exported function; the domain code reads no clock and no randomness (timestamps come from the list's own clock); it never throws and reports failures as data, with the reasons taken from the existing `Result` errors (no new error code).
